# Pipeline Execution (BC1 / BC4 / BC5)

- Interfaces → `get_backend().execute(graph)` only.
- `pipeline.py` / legacy shims: re-exports only — put logic in orchestrator / planner / node_executor / executor / checkpoint.
- IR: validate via `load_ir` / `dump_ir`; major version mismatch hard-fails.
- Modes: sequential (default), `parallel` (waves), streaming, event-driven (xor parallel), resume via `resume_run_id` + graph_hash.
- Conditions: AST whitelist only (`conditions.py`).
- Cache keys SHA-256; respect `cacheable` / checkpoints / `run_control` pause-cancel.
- Detail: `.kiro/steering/pipeline-execution.md`, `docs/PIPELINE_EXECUTION.md`.
